  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is implemented as planned, and the full test suite passes (1915 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't run a type checker or the manual `--set` check from the plan.\n\n- **Behavior:** it splits on the first `=`. So `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`. Input with no `=` or an empty key fails with `'x' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Code:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Docs:** I added entries to `docs/api.md`, `docs/parameter-types.md` and `CHANGES.md`.\n- **Tests:** there are new cases in `tests/test_types.py` and a `KeyValue` entry in `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nVersion 8.5.0 is already released, so I put the changelog entry under a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" heading and marked the class `versionadded:: 8.6`. Change both if you want a different version.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
